> On Tue, 21 February, 2006 5:49 pm, Takashi Iwai wrote:
> 
> > If you set INTERLEAVED flag in the pcm hardware setting, it seems not
> > matching with your hardware model.
> >
> >
> 
> Oddly, I set both. So I can fix that now. Not sure how I can execute two
> DMA transfers though - ie one to the left buffer and one to the right.
> Hmmm.

There are several possibilities.  One solution is to provide two
individual mono streams and let alsa-lib bind them.  This will require
less work in the kernel driver side.  The drawback is that this won't
work with kernel OSS emulation.

Another solution is to implement it in the driver, of course.
Even if the buffer assignment on your device is exotic, you can still
manage it by manually tuning the buffer pointers in hw_params callback
and set proper values in ioctl(SND_PCM_IOCTL1_CHANNEL_INFO).  An
example is korg1212 driver.


